   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {To analyze the local environmental discrepancy of different high-rise
   building regions in the Changsha City, three typical building regions
   are selected for measured. There are many measuring points of every
   region and every point is tested three days, three testing time segments
   in every day. For finding out the inner environmental difference of
   every tenement, a typical house is selected and tested. Meanwhile,
   infrared ray measurement is used to analyze the urban heat island effect
   of every region. Results show there is little environmental distinction
   among the different high-rise building regions, while the distinction of
   the indoor environmental status with different typical tenement in
   different building regions is large, due to the difference of the inner
   personnel movement and living habit. The analyses of the infrared ray
   may find out the intensity of the urban heat island effect in winter is
   upwards 6 degree centigrade, but the intensity is relatively less around
   the Yuelu Mountain. The analysis results can play a reference role in
   the constructing and planning of high-rise buildings in the future.},
