   Maritime Univ; IEEE EMC Romania Chapter; IEEE Signal Proc Romania
   Chapter; IEEE SMC Romania Chapter},
Abstract = {In the age of technology, stress makes its mark on people, prolonged
   states of anxiety can eventually lead to real dramas. This is the second
   study we made it on the recognition of fear/anxiety in relation to other
   emotions (happiness, fury, sadness, neutral tone, boredom and disgust)
   using Emo-DB. In the first study, we have applied K-Nearest Neighbour
   (KNN) classifier on spectral and cepstral features and we obtained an
   overall recognition rate 68.5\% {[}9]. The focus of this paper is to
   compare the previous results with those obtained with the DL-CNN Deep
   learning neural networks with convolutional layer. We used the same
   database Emo-DB, for the German language and we applied DL-CNN
   classifier on cepstral features which had converted into images. The
   fear emotion was recognized in percent of 77.5\% when the DL-CNN
   classifier use seven emotions, respectively 84.2\% when we have only two
   outputs for neural network (fear and other).},
