   Environm Canada; European Assoc Sci Air Pollut},
Abstract = {A three dimensional tool coupling the thermal energy balance of
   buildings and the modeling of the atmospheric flow in urban areas has
   been developed. In this work the effects of complexity in real urban
   geometry on the interaction between airflows and radiation exchanges
   with different surfaces is tested. The model results are encouraging and
   give insight into local surface-atmosphere processes, but further and
   more rigorous testing has to be performed with other datasets.},
