Abstract = {The paper firstly analyzes the characteristics of western urban
   governance, that is, advocating decentralization, emphasizing
   partnerships and multi-governance system,focusing on process guiding and
   regional guiding in decision-making. Then, the author discusses reasons
   for the changes in urban governance, that is, competitions between
   cities have led to entrepreneurial government action. With the weakening
   of the welfare system, government policies are changing. Due to the
   advancement of the democratization, residents have involved in urban
   governance. At the end of the paper, the enlightenment brought by
   western urban governance to China is discussed.},
