   AND ENVIRONMENT-FRIENDLY SOCIETY},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {214-218},
Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Urban ecosystem is an advanced man-made complex ecosystem consisted of
   nature, society and economy, and its health degree has vitally
   determined significance to urban sustainable development. In order to
   manage urban ecological environment effectively, it is necessary to
   implement the synthetic assessment of urban ecosystem health. Aiming at
   the problem of unknown standard value of health assessment, the
   synthetic health assessment index system and assessment model based on
   attribute theory were established. As a case study in
   Changsha-Zhuzhou-Xiangtan urban agglomeration with the above methods,
   the results showed that the health of this urban agglomeration belonged
   to moderate level. Based on further analysis, the health restricting
   factors were identified, and corresponding regulation measures were put
   forward. The results can offer some assistant decisions for this urban
   agglomeration ecological planning, as well as ``Two-oriented Society{''}
   construction.},
