   JAPAN, AUG, 1993},
Organization = {Appl Reg Sci Conf; Urban Reg Economists Grp Kansai, Japan},
Abstract = {This paper proposes a matrix called a benefit incidence matrix which
   represents the structure of benefit incidence derived from various urban
   development projects with special attention to a change in environmental
   quality. The matrix consists of the beneficiaries and cost sharers,
   expressed by columns, and the items of benefits and costs, expressed by
   rows. The associated (i, j) element of the matrix expresses the amount
   of benefits or costs with respect to the item (i) of the beneficiary or
   cost burdener (j), so that the social efficiency and equity of the
   project can easily be discussed.},
