Note = {International Conference on Tourism, Technology and Systems (ICOTTS),
   Cartagena, COLOMBIA, NOV 04-06, 2021},
Abstract = {Pilgrimage tourism, of which the Camino de Santiago is a notable
   example, has a significant social and economic impact and is therefore
   included in tourism planning activities. Given the economic and social
   importance of pilgrimage routes, it is important to examine pilgrim's
   satisfaction and emotions during their journey. Therefore, the main aim
   of this study is to examine pilgrims of the Camino de Santiago
   satisfaction and emotions. Based on a sample of 124 pilgrims of the
   Camino de Santiago, the results show that they are satisfied with the
   Camino, with the strongest emotions being happiness, joy and peace.
   These findings are important to support the management of pilgrimage
   routes.},
