Organization = {Springer Nature; Springer LNCS LNAI},
Abstract = {Detecting emotions from the speech is one of the emergent research
   fields in the area of human information processing. Expressing emotion
   is a very difficult task for a person with neurological disorder. Hence,
   a Speech Emotion Recognition (SER) system may solve this by ensuring a
   barrier-less communication. Various research has been carried out in the
   area of SER. Therefore, the main objective of this research is to
   develop a system that can recognize emotion from the speech of a
   neurologically disordered person. Since convolutional neural network
   (CNN) is an effective method, it has been considered to develop the
   system. The system uses tonal properties like MFCCs. RAVDESS audio
   speech and song databases for training and testing. In addition, a
   custom local dataset developed to support further training and testing.
   The performance of the proposed system compared with the traditional
   machine learning models as well as with the pre-trained CNN models
   including VGG16 and VGG19. The results demonstrate that the CNN model
   proposed in this research performed better than the mentioned machine
   learning techniques. This system enables one tohhhhhh classify eight
   emotions of neurologically disordered person including calm, angry,
   fearful, disgust, happy, surprise, neutral and sad.},
