Pages = {1114-1120},
Note = {Applied Energy Symposium and Forum - Low-Carbon Cities and Urban Energy
   Systems (CUE), Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 05-07, 2018},
Organization = {Appl Energy; Appl Energy Innovat Inst; Tongji Univ; China Assoc Sci \&
   Technol, HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile; Shanghai
   Key Lab Urban Regenerat \& Spatial Optimizat Technol; MOE Joint Lab Int
   Cooperat Eco Urban Design; Sichuan Univ; Shanghai Univ Electric Power;
   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {To promote the energy revolution strategy on the Chinese city level, we
   need to absorb and learn from the experience of the transformation and
   upgrading of urban energy systems in developed countries. The energy
   systems of different urban are related with its resources endowment,
   history, and policy environment, and also have the similar development
   regular. The study focused on analyzing comparatively the practice of
   supply, consumption, technology and mechanisms about energy system of
   the topical foreign cities, and put forward the existing problems of
   China's urban energy development. The results show that the top-level
   design of infrastructure construction and the cooperation of
   stakeholders are emphasized at the strategic planning level. In terms of
   energy utilization, we should maximize the use of clean energy inside
   and outside the city and focus on central heating and cooling. As for
   energy consumption, mandatory energy efficiency standards for energy
   consumption should be established and implemented, and we should
   increase energy conservation investment to build a service system for
   energy conservation measures. In terms of smart energy, the application
   of Internet and other technologies is to improve the control, security
   self healing and public service ability of urban energy. In the aspect
   of policy mechanism, the guidance of policy and economic incentive are
   to innovative participation model and promote the benefit of
   multi-party. Copyright 2018 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
