   Waseda Univ; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Urban tourism management is a systematic project which contains tourism
   marketing, tourism resources, tourism facilities, and tourism
   environment, etc. Based on the system theory, the authors of this paper
   tries to build a urban tourism system model, which includes tourist
   subsystems, tourism channel subsystems, tourism supply subsystems, and
   tourism environment subsystems. On the basis of this model, the urban
   tourism management framework were proposed so as to provide a more
   comprehensive and enforceable guidelines for urban tourism management
   departments in China. This framework mainly includes objectives and
   means. In the last part, a case study based on Beijing is carried out to
   evaluate subsystems, find out existing problems and provides solutions.},
