   Sarria, Barcelona, SPAIN, MAY, 2002},
Abstract = {The interrelated issues of urban sprawl, traffic congestion, noise, and
   air pollution are major socioeconomic problems faced by most European
   cities. A methodology is currently being developed for evaluating the
   role of green space and urban form in alleviating the adverse effects of
   urbanisation, mainly focusing on the environment but also accounting for
   socioeconomic aspects. The objectives and structure of the methodology
   are briefly outlined and illustrated with preliminary results obtained
   from case studies performed on several European cities. (C) 2004
