   Conf on Climate Changes, Global Warming, Biological Programs/1st WSEAS
   Int Conf on Natural Hazards, Bucharest, ROMANIA, NOV 07-09, 2008},
Organization = {WSEAS},
Abstract = {Considering the ecological approach, urban renewal planning involves the
   definition of a very mutual relationship between manufactured goods and
   the environment (in an extensive meaning) in which they lie and that
   modify; in the same time, that means to build a new landscape and to
   transform the territory in an indelible way. This awareness, perhaps not
   so evident in a more widespread construction and planning practice, is a
   disciplinary postulate that always characterized the responsible
   architectural and planning processes.
   It is necessary to deepen an assessment procedure able to synthesize the
   plurality and complexity of themes that a renewal plan involves, in
   order to provide an instrument to support the decisions of planners,
   stakeholders and administrators.
   The paper explores briefly the global context about urban regeneration,
   than deepens some cultural aspects regarding the ecological approach,
   than analyses the regulatory apparatus in force in Italy, and finally
   presents a research results about integrated evaluation process of
   renewal masterplan applied in three ex-industrial areas sited in Pavia.},
