   Singapore, SINGAPORE, OCT, 2011},
Organization = {Singapore Inst Elect (SIE)},
Abstract = {In this paper, we propose a recognition model of multi-emotion states
   from electroencephalogram (EEG) based on Bayesian Networks. The
   subjects' emotion states (anger, happiness, and neutral) are elicited by
   using emotional videos along with collecting EEG signals from fourteen
   channels around the scalp. We use Receiver Operating Characteristic
   (ROC) to select input features of this model from power spectrum values
   of fifty six frequency bands of fourteen-channel EEG signals with each
   being divided into four bands. Experimental results show that the
   proposed model performs well and using EEG to detect multi-emotion
   states is feasible. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and/or
   peer-review under responsibility of the Organizers of 2011 International
   Conference on Energy and Environmental Science.},
