Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {Numerous studies have explored psychophysical dimensions of visual and
   audio perceptions. However, establishing a unified framework to
   elucidate the psychophysical dimensions of tactile perception remains
   challenging. The vocabulary used varies among researchers and the same
   terms may imply different meanings. Establishing consistent terminology
   can overcome obstacles in psychophysical studies of tactile perception.
   In addition, creating a logical and comprehensive semantic system is the
   first step in designing advanced tactile interaction. This study
   proposes psychophysical dimensions of tactile perception by classifying
   vocabularies representing tactile perception based on affective
   engineering and haptics. We compiled vocabulary related to tactile
   perception and proposed two classification criteria to systematically
   classify them. Criteria based on affective engineering approaches and
   those proposed by previous researchers on object properties were
   combined to derive eight psychophysical dimensions of tactile
   perception. The relationships between vocabularies in different studies
   were discerned, laying the groundwork for consistent terminology.},
