   Assoc Sci \& Technol Jiaxing City; Zhejiang Univ, Dept Psychol; Hope
   Coll; Western Illinois Univ; Jacksonville State Univ; Unilever Co},
Abstract = {Recent research has revealed that social identity has an effect on
   people's emotions, but little is known about how it works in an online
   context. This study explores how the social identity of online game
   groups impact positive and negative emotions. Social Identity Rating
   Scale of the Online Game Groups, the Online Gaming Addiction Scale of
   Undergraduates, and PANAS were applied to 699 online game players.
   Results indicate that the social identity of online game groups have a
   significant effect on both positive affect and negative affect, and
   online gaming addiction plays a moderator between the social identity of
   the online game groups and negative affect.},
