Abstract = {This paper focuses on the issue of vitality in urban public spaces,
   streets in particular, as a major indicator of their success. The study
   first provides a theoretical framework for understanding the social
   value and role of urban public spaces on quality of urban life; second,
   it discusses the essential components of vitality in streets. Finally,
   investigating vitality and its determinants in two major streets in
   Famagusta and Kyrenia, North Cyprus, the paper highlights the issues of
