   Commun Res \& Act; European Community Psychol Assoc; Amer Psychol Assoc
   Div 27 Soc Commun Res \& Act},
Abstract = {Over the past years an ample number of self-compassionate interventions
   have been developed within a variety of psychotherapy approaches such as
   Compassion-focused therapy or Emotion-focused therapy (EFT). The goal of
   this review is to contribute to a deeper understanding on
   self-compassionate interventions in EFT, principles of EFT, and
   self-compassion definitions. In EFT self-compassion capacities are
   developed through the therapeutic relationship and self-soothing
   dialogues. Promoting self-compassion improves clients' ability to soothe
   and validate their painful experiences. Future research in EFT will need
   to continue to examine the therapeutic process and outcome of
   self-compassion interventions by exploring ways on how to measure the
   in-session improvement of clients' self-compassion capabilities.},
